<DataShopLayout current="ecosystem" title="The Dharmic Data System | DATA" description="How DATA, the atlas, decision tools, and public build notes fit together.">
  <section class="page-hero system-hero">
    <p class="overline">The bigger picture</p>
    <h1>One method.<br />Different objects.</h1>
    <p>Dharmic Data is building a family of tools for better orientation: find the signal, inspect the context, choose a next move, and preserve what you learned.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="system-map" aria-label="Dharmic Data ecosystem">
    <article class="system-core"><p>Dharmic Data</p><h2>Orient → inspect → decide → preserve</h2></article>
    <a href="/atlas/"><span>01 / Explore</span><h2>Atlases</h2><p>Interactive context for a place, image, community, or contested story.</p><b>Open Atlas 001 →</b></a>
    <a href="/shop/"><span>02 / Carry</span><h2>DATA editions</h2><p>Textiles and physical records that let cultural memory travel.</p><b>View Dossier 001 →</b></a>
    <a href="https://dharmicdata.org/"><span>03 / Decide</span><h2>Decision tools</h2><p>Evidence-led guidance for finding the first AI project worth building.</p><b>Visit Dharmic Data →</b></a>
    <a href="https://dharmicdata.org/projects/"><span>04 / Prove</span><h2>Public builds</h2><p>Working examples, explicit limits, and reusable lessons from the build.</p><b>See the work →</b></a>
  </section>
  <section class="flywheel">
    <div><p class="overline">The operating loop</p><h2>Research becomes software. Software becomes an artifact. The artifact brings new people back to the research.</h2></div>
    <ol>
      <li><span>1</span>Find a culturally specific signal.</li>
      <li><span>2</span>Map the context and source material.</li>
      <li><span>3</span>Publish an edition with a bounded decision.</li>
      <li><span>4</span>Archive the story and learn from the response.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</DataShopLayout>
